{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794746474,"nonce":"Bpk2DmHnZHzvCcTvw0velqxSch4=","message":"Where generics are used at concrete types, measured on the Haxe unit suite (f7b29f52; `inst_report program.tast`, 0.03 s).\n\n1008 specializable instances at 11561 call and new sites; 27 uses left unresolved. 259 of the instances (4180 sites) pass a value type, which HashLink boxes when it erases the parameter. 174 generic classes are instantiated at concrete arguments.\n\nThe value-type instances that matter most for the rows we trail: haxe.ds.StringMap.get\u003cInt\u003e and set\u003cInt\u003e, IntMap.get\u003cInt\u003e and set\u003cInt\u003e and new\u003cInt\u003e (the Map\u003cString, Int\u003e shape knucleotide uses), Array.push\u003cInt\u003e, Array.copy\u003cInt\u003e, Array.sort\u003cInt\u003e, Lambda.array\u003cInt\u003e, and haxe.IMap.get\u003cK=Int, V=Int\u003e (through the interface, so the receiver's arguments are found by walking its supertypes). The test helper unit.Test.eq\u003cInt\u003e dominates the count, which says more about the suite than about programs.\n\nHow it works: it starts from every function that is not generic and follows calls and `new` into generic code. At each site it reads the class arguments from the receiver (upcasting through superclasses and interfaces) and the method arguments by matching the declared signature against the type of the callee as used. A specialized body is walked with those arguments in place, so a generic that calls another at its own parameter is found: in the fixture, Pair.new\u003cString, Int\u003e is found only inside Pair.swap\u003cInt, String\u003e. Arguments that stay unbound or nest past six levels are left to the erased copy, and the count is a lower bound by design: the erased copy always exists, so a missed instance is a missed optimization, never a wrong result.\n\nStill to do before this pays off: lower bodies at all (nothing consumes these instances yet), and the policy for which instances to specialize (value-type arguments first; reference-type arguments only where a constraint devirtualizes).","files":null}]}